# P1a-CTL2 (CONDITIONAL, runs when P1a-CTL has NO-VERDICT): the same arm on the WINDOW image (CONTROL audited profile, flags off, which S0-CTL proves byte-identical to production), arm timeout raised.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the combined development window (docs/tp4-combined-window.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2-levern-prefix and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the NEEDS graph, the swap
# rules and every read and cutover rule. ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2ln-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed branch commit; every window job serves it. The jobs named
# CTL (and T0, G0) run the PRODUCTION base image tp4-serve-10, driven from a throwaway commit of ship/262k-prefix that also carries the one-line S2_TIMEOUTS change of ORDER.txt.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2ln-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=exactness-shared
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
